[Music]  hey everyone welcome to another  installment of harry potter theory today  we're going to be discussing you guessed  it monsters  now in the past i've made several videos  discussing various magical creatures and  i almost always refer to these creatures  as well creatures or beasts but today  we're going to be discussing a very  different type of beast we're going to  be discussing the monsters of the  wizarding world that is beasts so  horrifying that they warrant their own  terminology but we're not just going to  be discussing any old monsters we're  going to be tackling and listing off all  the known monsters found within the  monster book of monsters if you aren't  familiar with the monster book of  monsters well allow me to jog your  memory the book properly comes to our  attention quite early on in the story  when hagrid supplies harry with the book  for his 13th birthday  he gives harry the book because it's a  requirement for his third year at  hogwarts more specifically it's a  required textbook for the care of  magical creatures class the book was  written by wizard named eduardus lima  sometime before 1932  and serves as a tome for  magisterologists  however few there may be  known for its volatile nature the book  is exceedingly difficult to open  primarily due to the fact that it'll try  to bite the reader's fingers off how do  we open our books malfoy repeated he  took out his copy of the monster book of  monsters which he had bound shut with a  length of rope other people took theirs  out too  some like harry had belted their books  shut  others had crammed them inside tight  bags or clamped them together with  binder clips hasn't hasn't anyone been  able to open their books said hagrid  looking crestfallen  the class all shook their heads you've  got to stroke them said hagrid as though  this was the most obvious thing in the  world  look  so provided that the book itself is a  kind of monster i can't help but wonder  what lies within  are these monsters as bad as the book  would suggest let's dive into it number  one alazor of westacottus  alazor of westacottus was a magical  creature with a round torso long spindly  limbs large feet large round ears and a  long pointed nose  in my opinion alizor almost looks like a  mix between a goblin from harry potter  and gollum from lord of the rings in the  monster book of monsters alazor of  westacottus is depicted with the snarl  wearing a pointed helmet  2. coco rumsey catcher the coco ramsay  catcher is a small humanoid magical  creature that resembles a cornish pixie  in appearance it's likely that they come  from the same family of creatures not  much can be said of the coco rumsey  catcher other than that they appear to  enjoy picking flowers  number three doralesnov frieza the  doralesnoff freezer was a humanoid  magical creature with large bulging eyes  and pointed ears  i can only assume based on the  appearance of the doralesnoff freezer  that they are somehow related to house  elves and goblins  4. manticore the manticore notably  originates from persian mythology and  was later adopted by the greeks and  medieval europeans  the manticore can best be described by  major zoologist nuke scamander the  manticore is a highly dangerous greek  beast with the head of a man the body of  a lion and the tail of a scorpion  as dangerous as the chimera and is rare  the manticore is reputed to croon softly  as it devours its prey  manticore skin repels almost all known  charms and the sting causes instant  death  the manticore is also referenced by  hermione granger in the prisoner of  azgaban speaking to its savagery a  manticore savaged someone in 1296 and  they let the manticore off  oh no that was only because everyone was  too scared to go near it  i think that the manticore is truly  befitting the title of monster  5. greenwort goth the green wart golf is  in my opinion the scariest looking  creature from this list  in appearance the green wart goth  resembles a sort of devilish looking  troll  it sports long horns on its head small  bat-like wings on its back and  two-fingered claw-like hands  6. hippogriff hippogriffs are likely one  of the only monsters you've actually  heard of on this list magical beasts  that have the front legs wings and heads  of a giant eagle and the torso behind  legs and tail of a horse  they come in all sorts of colors  including stormy grey bronze pinkish  rhone gleaming chestnut and inky black  hippogriffs were dangerous carnivorous  creatures but could be trained by the  right witch or wizard  hagrid discusses the hippogryph in great  detail during one of his lessons now  first thing you've got to know about  hippogriffs is they're proud easily  offended hippogriffs are don't never  insult one because it might be the last  thing you do  you always wait for the hippogriff to  make the first move it's polite see you  walk towards him and you bow and you  wait if he bows back you're allowed to  touch him if he doesn't bow then get  away from him sharpish because those  talons hurt  at one stage in the harry potter books  and films we're introduced to buckpeak a  hippogriff that hagrid introduces to  students in his care for magical  creatures class however buckbeak didn't  exactly have the same relationship with  all of the students  harry for example was able to ride beak  but draco didn't have the same  experience  draco ends up taunting buckbeak to which  he receives an injury completely furious  draco ends up trying to get buckbeak  killed with the hippogriff eventually  being sentenced to death by the ministry  of magic  fortunately buck peak is eventually  saved by harry hermione and the time  turner 7. limax the limax was a magical  creature with a snake-like lower body  frog-like head and four arms they are  known for being able to wield a variety  of weapons at once it's likely that the  limax's name is inspired by genus of  air-breathing land slugs that share the  same name  8. maraf lal dendi  marath lal dendi was a magical creature  resembling a humanoid-like plant with  roots  due to its similarities in appearance to  a mandrake another magical sentient  plant resembling humans  it's likely that they're from the same  family  9. nasal mumps nasal mumps are magical  creatures which resemble both cornish  pixies and the coco rumsey catcher the  most obvious differences are a lack of  wings and a much rounder belly they also  look even more menacing if that's  possible  10. chiliphoras drogodflicarus i know i  said earlier the eliza of westacottus  resembles gollum from lord of the rings  but i think that the chiliphorous drugod  flickerus resembles him even more  despite the wings however there is one  massive distinction here the chaliferous  dragonflickerus is only the size of a  quill this humanoid creature had round  deep set eyes around belly and large  flat feet 11. sphinx you guys must know  this one already that is as long as  you've read the books fantastic beasts  and where to find them published by newt  scamander describes the sphinx as  follows  the egyptian sphinx has a human head on  a lion's body for over a thousand years  it has been used by witches and wizards  to guard valuables and secret hideaways  highly intelligent the sphinx delights  in puzzles and riddles it is usually  dangerous only when what it is guarding  is threatened 12. troll of nadroge the  troll of nadraj was a breed of troll  sharing the troll name along with river  trolls mountain trolls and forest trolls  the troll of nadroge is very similar in  appearance to a mountain troll but  differs in that they possess huge hands  with clawed disproportionately long  fingers  13. valkor  valkors were humanoid-like creatures of  immense size that were able to rip  entire trees out of the ground with ease  apparently a standard valkorm is  approximately eight times the size of a  normal adult human which is scary if we  consider the fact that they are  extremely hostile towards humans  valkors have large heads covered in  blunt thorns thin arms and thick legs  and that's it for this video had you  heard of all these creatures which ones  were new to you  leave a comment down below and as always  if you enjoyed the content please  consider liking the video and  subscribing to the channel until next  time remember  if you listen carefully enough the past  whispers to you  [Music]  you

